Id: sctl001w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set kern.randompid=1 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl.conf(5); sysctl(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

kern.randompid is 0, so process IDs are handed out in order: one
process's ID tells the next. Predictable IDs help whoever races a
process to its temporary files or signals it, and FreeBSD randomises
them unless told not to:
  # sysctl -w kern.randompid=1
and keep it in /etc/sysctl.conf.
